@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Compress Image Online Free";
    ViewData["Description"] = "Compress JPG, PNG, or WebP images online for free. Reduce file size without losing quality. Fast and secure image compression tool.";
    Layout = "~/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml";
}

<head>
    <meta name="description" content="@ViewData["Description"]" />
    <meta name="keywords" content="compress image, reduce image size, jpg compressor, png compressor, webp compressor, image optimizer online" />
    <meta name="author" content="RatPDF" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://ratpdf.com/PDF/ImageCompressor" />
</head>

<div class="container py-5">
    <div class="card shadow-lg p-4" style="border-radius:15px;">
        <div class="card-body text-center">

            <img src="~/images/ratpdf-logo.png" height="60" class="mb-3" />
            <h1 class="fw-bold mb-3">Image Compressor</h1>
            <p class="text-muted mb-2">Compress JPG, PNG, or WebP images instantly without losing visible quality.</p>
            <span id="imageUsageBadge" class="badge bg-secondary mb-3" data-image-tool-id="imagecompress">3 free use(s) today</span>

            <div class="mb-3">
                <input type="file" id="imageInput" class="form-control" accept="image/png, image/jpeg, image/webp">
            </div>

            <div class="d-grid gap-2 d-md-flex justify-content-md-center mb-3">
                <button class="btn btn-primary" onclick="compressImageAction()">Compress</button>
                <button class="btn btn-outline-secondary" onclick="clearAll()">Clear</button>
            </div>
            <div id="outputSection" class="mt-4 d-none">
                <p class="fw-bold">Original Size: <span id="originalSize"></span></p>
                <p class="fw-bold">Compressed Size: <span id="compressedSize"></span></p>

                <img id="previewImg" class="img-fluid mb-3" style="max-height:300px; border:1px solid #ccc;" />

                <div class="d-grid gap-2 d-md-flex justify-content-md-center">
                    <a id="downloadLink" class="btn btn-success" download="compressed_image.jpg">Download Compressed Image</a>
                    <button class="btn btn-secondary" onclick="copyBase64()">Copy Base64</button>
                </div>

                <textarea id="base64Output" class="form-control mt-3" rows="4" readonly></textarea>
            </div>

            <div id="errorBox" class="alert alert-danger d-none mt-3"></div>
            <section class="related-tools">
                <h3>Related Tools</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><a href="/PDF/Compress">Compress PDF</a></li>
                </ul>
            </section>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="container py-5">
     <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-5">Step-by-Step Guide: How to Compress Images Online</h3>
            <ol class="text-start mb-4">
                <li><strong>Upload your image:</strong> Click the upload box or drag and drop your JPG, PNG, or WebP image.</li>
                <li><strong>Click Compress:</strong> The tool instantly reduces your file size without noticeable quality loss.</li>
                <li><strong>Preview your compressed image:</strong> View the smaller file and check its quality.</li>
                <li><strong>Download or copy Base64:</strong> Save the compressed image or copy its Base64 for web use.</li>
            </ol>

            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Why Use Our Online Image Compressor?</h3>
            <ul class="text-start mb-4">
                <li>✔ <strong>Free and browser-based:</strong> Compress images instantly without installing software.</li>
                <li>✔ <strong>High-quality compression:</strong> Reduce file size while preserving visible image quality.</li>
                <li>✔ <strong>Supports multiple formats:</strong> JPG, PNG, and WebP images are all supported.</li>
                <li>✔ <strong>Secure and private:</strong> Your images never leave your browser; no files are stored on our servers.</li>
                <li>✔ <strong>Cross-platform:</strong> Works on Windows, Mac, Android, and iOS devices.</li>
                <li>✔ <strong>Fast and convenient:</strong> Compress single or multiple images in seconds.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Use Cases for Image Compression</h3>
            <p class="text-start">
                Image compression is useful in many scenarios for personal, business, and web purposes:
            </p>
            <ul class="text-start mb-4">
                <li><strong>Website Optimization:</strong> Reduce image sizes to improve page load speed, user experience, and SEO rankings.</li>
                <li><strong>Email Attachments:</strong> Shrink large image files to send via email without size restrictions.</li>
                <li><strong>Social Media Sharing:</strong> Compress images for faster uploads on platforms like Instagram, Facebook, or Twitter.</li>
                <li><strong>Archiving:</strong> Save storage space on your device by reducing the size of high-resolution photos.</li>
                <li><strong>Design Projects:</strong> Optimize graphics and mockups for faster preview and easier collaboration.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Benefits of Compressing Images Online</h3>
            <p class="text-start">
                Using our image compressor has multiple advantages:
            </p>
            <ul class="text-start mb-4">
                <li><strong>Improved Website Performance:</strong> Smaller images load faster, reducing bounce rates and improving SEO.</li>
                <li><strong>Storage Savings:</strong> Reduce file sizes without sacrificing quality, freeing up space on devices and cloud storage.</li>
                <li><strong>Easy Sharing:</strong> Compressed images are easier to share via email or messaging apps.</li>
                <li><strong>Convenience:</strong> No software installation required; compress images directly in your browser.</li>
                <li><strong>Privacy:</strong> All processing is client-side, keeping your images secure and private.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Advanced Tips for Image Compression</h3>
            <ul class="text-start mb-4">
                <li>Resize images to desired dimensions before compression to achieve smaller file sizes.</li>
                <li>Adjust quality parameters for JPG compression (0.5–0.8) for optimal balance between size and quality.</li>
                <li>Use WebP format for maximum compression efficiency while retaining high quality.</li>
                <li>Compress multiple images one by one for best results, then combine them using related tools like “Images to PDF.”</li>
                <li>Always preview compressed images to ensure the output quality meets your requirements.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h3>
            <div class="text-start mb-4">
                <p><strong>Q1: How do I compress images online?</strong></p>
                <p>Upload your JPG, PNG, or WebP image and click 'Compress' to reduce its file size instantly.</p>

                <p><strong>Q2: Can I compress multiple image formats?</strong></p>
                <p>Yes, our tool supports JPG, PNG, and WebP images for compression.</p>

                <p><strong>Q3: Does compression reduce image quality?</strong></p>
                <p>No. The tool uses optimized compression to reduce file size while preserving visible image quality.</p>

                <p><strong>Q4: Do I need to register or install software?</strong></p>
                <p>No registration or installation is required; the tool is completely free and works in your browser.</p>

                <p><strong>Q5: Can I use this tool on mobile devices?</strong></p>
                <p>Yes, the Image Compressor works on Windows, Mac, Android, and iOS devices.</p>

                <p><strong>Q6: Why should I compress images?</strong></p>
                <p>Compressing images reduces file size, improves website performance, saves storage space, and makes sharing faster and easier.</p>

                <p><strong>Q7: Which formats are best for compression?</strong></p>
                <p>JPG is ideal for photos, PNG for images with transparency, and WebP for efficient compression with high quality.</p>
            </div>

            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Conclusion</h3>
            <p class="text-start">
                Compressing images online has never been easier. Our free tool allows you to reduce the size of JPG, PNG, and WebP files without compromising visible quality. 
                Whether you are optimizing a website, sending email attachments, or archiving photos, RatPDF’s Image Compressor provides fast, secure, and reliable compression directly in your browser.
            </p>
            <p class="text-start">
                Try it today to save space, improve performance, and streamline your workflow. With no registration, no downloads, and full privacy, our online image compressor is the perfect solution for anyone who needs high-quality, optimized images instantly.
            </p>
</div>

